      "id": "simple-path-to-wealth-s010-p00287",
      "source_en": "In referencing the market’s performance in this chapter, you may have noticed I jump between using the Dow and the S&P as the indexes. I prefer the S&P because it is broader and therefore a bit more precise. But the Dow goes back further in history and is more useful (and available) for the long view. If you overlay their charts over time, they track together with remarkable consistency, making them, for our purposes, indistinguishable.",
